{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/371304-immortal-covers","id":371304,"title":"Immortal Covers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-15T12:16:38-08:00","id":371304,"title":"Immortal Covers","content":"So I was looking through Immortals when I came up with the question what would happen if a Demon made a Soul Pact with one of the humans from that book and cashed it in for a Cover.<br /> <br /> I figured for the more &quot;standard&quot; immortals like Blood Bathers, Wardens, Patchwork People, Eternals, and Harvesters. It would act like a normal cover as long as they stayed in character (Blood Bathers carrying out their ritual, Wardens staying in their territory, Eternals protecting the item they are bound to, etc, etc). Although some of these have unique powers, due to the scale of these powers letting Demons use them wouldn't be game breaking would it? or would you require the Demons get the Show of Power Exploit?<br /> <br /> Purified I figured would be treated like one would treat a Vampire or Werewolf cover. As in people think you are a Purified, but you can't actually use their powers unless you use &quot;Show of Power&quot;<br /> <br /> But I got stumped when it came to the Body Thieves, Visitors and Reborn. How would you guys handle these ones?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T13:03:11-08:00","id":371375,"title":"","content":"Demons get no benefit from acquiring Cover from other supernaturals. In fact, it hurts them based on how much Supernatural Potency they have. The only thing they get is the human identity who was the &quot;base&quot; of that person. They acquire no powers with the Cover, and it only accounts for what they were <i>without</i> the supernatural portion tacked on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T13:28:28-08:00","id":371394,"title":"","content":"Makes sense, so in this case the only being that would hurt the Demon is the Purified. The others don't have a Supernatural Potency trait.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T17:03:42-08:00","id":371558,"title":"","content":"I would handle them like any other supernatural, with all the appropriate rules, including the use of Show of Power to use abilities not normally available to a Demon.<br /> <br /> As a Storyteller, I would also keep an eye on anyone who took a Patchwork Person as a Cover since they always struck me as an Immortal that likely has close ties to the God-Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T01:00:35-08:00","id":372087,"title":"","content":"I hope something involving Pacts and Covers with other Supernaturals (greater or minor templated) is covered in the Storytellers Guide thats currently being written. <br /> <br /> I don't expect a Demon to ever be able to properly steal a major supernatural's full set of abilities. I just think its a cool idea to appear as that supernatural and hide inside a secret society that has its own reasons for staying secret. Kinda like doubling up on security. Presuming the the GM does not take an interest in said supernatural communities activities. <br /> <br /> Basically, a few more embeds that let you pull of the trick of appearing as another Sup would be handy.<br /> <br /> Likewise a form of pact that might give you certain extended abilities e.g. spoofing against aura detection to appear as a Vampire for example. Or gain a cover that is &quot;immortal&quot; in so far as it won't age to death if they Pact with a Vampire for example. <br /> <br /> I suspect most of this stuff will be embeds and exploits though, not Pacts, a bit like Ephemeral Cover works out of the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T01:13:24-08:00","id":372095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/371304-immortal-covers?p=372087#post372087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't expect a Demon to ever be able to properly steal a major supernatural's full set of abilities. I just think its a cool idea to appear as that supernatural and hide inside a secret society that has its own reasons for staying secret. Kinda like doubling up on security. Presuming the the GM does not take an interest in said supernatural communities activities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends largely on the society and creatures.<br /> <br /> Pretty much anything that's a mover and shaker is going to be targeted by the GM or it's cults to help with projects. Supernatural communities tend to carve out these areas for themselves as a matter of course.<br /> <br /> Magi and Kindred are the ones that come to mind but really anything is fair game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 01-16-2015, 04:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T01:20:12-08:00","id":372099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/371304-immortal-covers?p=372087#post372087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, a few more embeds that let you pull of the trick of appearing as another Sup would be handy.<br /> <br /> Likewise a form of pact that might give you certain extended abilities e.g. spoofing against aura detection to appear as a Vampire for example.<br /> <br /> [\u2026]I suspect most of this stuff will be embeds and exploits though, not Pacts, a bit like Ephemeral Cover works out of the core.</div> </div> </div> </div>Deep Cover specifically applies its effect as an alternative that comes up whenever you could spoof.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T01:38:54-08:00","id":372109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/371304-immortal-covers?p=372099#post372099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Deep Cover specifically applies its effect as an alternative that comes up whenever you could spoof.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh...so it does. I really need to reread the players guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T13:27:31-08:00","id":372831,"title":"","content":"Hey guys!<br /> <br /> Thanks for all the good points! After going back and reading all the sections and powers mentioned in this thread, I can see the problems with my errant thought.<br /> <br /> Although like Hawthorn's suggestion of an Embed/Exploit, that let a Demon patch in minor supernatural tricks that don't &quot;do&quot; anything to a cover. Like &quot;unaging&quot; for example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/371304-immortal-covers?p=371558#post371558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would handle them like any other supernatural, with all the appropriate rules, including the use of Show of Power to use abilities not normally available to a Demon.<br /> <br /> As a Storyteller, I would also keep an eye on anyone who took a Patchwork Person as a Cover since they always struck me as an Immortal that likely has close ties to the God-Machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>On that point, I actually really like the idea that the Patchwork People are tied to the God-Machine and the clinics where the Patchwork People go to renew immortality being heavily protected Infrastructure. I'd personally would make it so it was only as difficult to get a Patchwork Person as a Cover as difficult as getting a regular Pact (especially since Patchwork people don't have any powers that would need spoofing. They just don't need sleep nor fall unconscious, they even age, the process just reverses it).<br /> <br /> Maintaining the Cover could be a fun side or main goal for a chronicle because the Demon would be taking Compromise rolls for not walking into the heart of the Infrastructure and letting the GM agents perform surgery on their cover. I can see a whole Agency forming to suborn and defend the Infrastructure that makes these Covers possible. On the other hand said Agency could also be Integrators turning other Demons over to the God-Machine, or just an Angel trying to trick Demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T16:06:33-08:00","id":372987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Afro Luigi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/371304-immortal-covers?p=372831#post372831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On that point, I actually really like the idea that the Patchwork People are tied to the God-Machine and the clinics where the Patchwork People go to renew immortality being heavily protected Infrastructure. I'd personally would make it so it was only as difficult to get a Patchwork Person as a Cover as difficult as getting a regular Pact (especially since Patchwork people don't have any powers that would need spoofing. They just don't need sleep nor fall unconscious, they even age, the process just reverses it).<br /> <br /> Maintaining the Cover could be a fun side or main goal for a chronicle because the Demon would be taking Compromise rolls for not walking into the heart of the Infrastructure and letting the GM agents perform surgery on their cover. I can see a whole Agency forming to suborn and defend the Infrastructure that makes these Covers possible. On the other hand said Agency could also be Integrators turning other Demons over to the God-Machine, or just an Angel trying to trick Demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quoted for truth! Yes, I agree wholeheartedly. I even had a story in my Demon game where they had to investigate a Patchwork Person after one of them became aware of his ticking heart. They make perfect God-Machine plot hooks for Mortals to investigate also. (I plan to use one in my Hunter the Vigil game shortly.) There's just so much you can do with them! I'm fond of the Visitors for similar reasons. Although technically spirits, Visitors are fun in that they are heavily tied to much more modern conspiracy theories, though I tend to think of them as disruptive elements (or possible suped up cryptids) in the God-Machine's plans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T21:41:26-08:00","id":373303,"title":"","content":"Well, demons don't get the benefits of another supernatural template, but in 2d ed not every supernatural character is a template, claimed are now a condition for example.<br /> <br /> Some of the types in immortals are ripe for being treated as conditions, since some of them don't even bar them from having unseen senses according to the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T22:56:23-08:00","id":373334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/371304-immortal-covers?p=373303#post373303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, demons don't get the benefits of another supernatural template, but in 2d ed not every supernatural character is a template, claimed are now a condition for example.<br /> <br /> Some of the types in immortals are ripe for being treated as conditions, since some of them don't even bar them from having unseen senses according to the book.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ohhh, that is something I would have never have thought of, despite the fact I was just studying 2nd Ed Claimed yesterday!<br /> <br /> Off the top of my head<ul><li>Blood Bathers are just performing a ritual to grant themselves a Unaging Condition for a variable time frame (depends on the ritual).</li> <li>Patchwork People have the Clockwork Heart Persistent Condition that needs to be refreshed every decade</li> <li>Reborn would probably have to be represented with a series of Conditions depending on how much they remember of previous lives.</li> </ul>The others would need more work, but that is a fun idea! =D","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If I post any good ideas regarding house rules feel free to use them! Giving me credit is optional! All I want is people to have fun!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4737-afro-luigi","name":"Afro Luigi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4737_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T10:20:49-08:00","id":375342,"title":"","content":"And the Visitors are all Claimed by a particularly <i>odd</i> group of &quot;Ephemeral&quot; Beings. <hr /><br /> For this, I'm assuming that you're using Mirrors' rules for aging (Every 5 years after 30, trade a dot in a Physical attribute for 2xp, which you may only spend on Social merits. Yeah, I'm aware that means that you're losing XP - it's a quick hack to GMC.)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Clockwork Heart [Persistent]</b></span><br /> Your heart has been bolstered and connected to an exceptionally complicated piece of clockwork, which metes out a steady pulse of life-filled energies. As long as the machine keeps running, you don't require sleep and cannot fall unconscious - you automatically succeed on the Stamina + Resolve roll to avoid falling unconscious upon having your health levels filled with Bashing or Lethal damage. In addition, your body may accept transplants from any donor without fear of tissue rejection.<br /> Of course, this all has a downside; your heart <i>needs</i> that little device. If this Condition is resolved for any reason, you begin to suffer cardiac arrest, taking 1A a minute, which only stops if you regain this Condition or get some <i>really</i> speedy treatment.<br /> <b>Caused By:</b> Surgical implantation, rewinding the clock.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> N/A<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Your heart stops; you are impaled through the heart.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Rejuvenation Clinic</span></b><br /> A Rejuvenation Clinic specializes in large-scale tissue replacement, with that tissue usually coming from people who've &quot;disappeared.&quot; The doctors that work there are usually the top of their field; the halls are comfortable and the operating theatres are nice and sterile.<br /> Among their many services, receiving care in a clinic quadruples healing times and can remove Tilts caused by Aggravated damage. However, their &quot;best&quot; procedure is rejuvenation - they implant you with a clockwork heart, double-check to see that everything is working properly, and replace old body parts with those from unwilling &quot;donors&quot;.<br /> <br /> The end result is essentially an entirely new body (or, at least, one with a few new parts) - it still ages normally, but the process reverses 10 or more years worth of aging - depending on how much of their body is replaced - which restores any dots in Physical attributes lost during that time. It also allows the patient's player to rearrange their Physical attributes and to reassign any Striking Looks they may have. It's also a reasonably good excuse to buy up merits such as Striking Looks or Giant that are normally only available during character creation.<br /> <br /> Characters with the Clockwork Heart condition are protected from most mundane tissue rejection, but even they have issues with having large portions of their body replaced. Their exceptional ability to accommodate foreign tissue means that they don't suffer any problems at all for the first decade, though wear and tear means that they have to get a &quot;tune up&quot; at least once a decade - being late for an appointment means they take 1B every month, which can only heal once they've gone back to the clinic and have had their parts replaced.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 01-19-2015, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T11:16:32-08:00","id":375400,"title":"","content":"Technically, the heart isn't replaced by a clockwork device, but the device is implanted as a sort of pacemaker. Also, the clockwork heart doesn't seem to need any rewinding according to the original rules, but the heart stopping due to other mystical sources would be fair game.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, even while a full body transplant (except the brain and spinal column) is possible, I don't think they always replace everything at once. New internal organs could probably last longer than exterior features, if someone wants to keep looking young. And if you'd replace enough, reversing more than 10 years worth of aging should be possible.<br /> <br /> Finally you could clarify that the timer for tissue rejection is reset after each tuning at the clinic. I understand why you didn't mention this, as you assumed that the body would aways be replaced in whole, which means that this timer reset is not necessary.<br /> <br /> I would just remove the part about transplants without clockwork hearts, as it isn't really related to the rest. Especially as the one year limit is arbitrary and as immunosurppressants (which are not necessary for those with a clockwork heart) have their own problems, as they surpress the immune system.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I forgot to mention that I like your idea amechra, even though I have all these comments. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":304,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","user":"Penta","date":". 01-19-2015, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T12:42:32-08:00","id":375472,"title":"","content":"True enough on the rejection stuff. I'll go ahead and remove that.<br /> <br /> And <i>fine</i>, I'll make it closer to the original; it was a quick 5-minute job anyway.<br /> <br /> I think I'll brush it up and post it on the general forum, since it isn't <i>exactly</i> Demon related.<br /> <br /> (And I'm glad you like it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}